{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Open Source Movement", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Open Source Software.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "acquisition", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of obtaining something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They promote the acquisition of software without paying it for it, and without the limitation of copyright.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "copyright", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ownership of something in a legal way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They promote the acquisition of software without paying it for it, and without the limitation of copyright.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feature", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a relevant characteristic of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It allows users to work on it to fix mistakes, add some features, and create variations of a piece of software.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "movement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "group of individuals that share a common interest and work together to achieve it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There were other cofounders but Raymond connects  the most with the movement because he's the main theorist on the matter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "accomplishment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something achieved in a skillful way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What are the accomplishments they got so far?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hacker", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an individual with advanced knowledge and skills on computer programing and software development", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They're also, along with the SFS, one of the main defenders of the hacker community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about the Open Source Movement. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a concept map explaining the important aspects of the Open Source Movement. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Show your concept map with your classmates and discuss about it.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research about the Open Source Movement. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a concept map to show the relevant characteristics of this company. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my ideas about the Open Source Movement with my classmates through a concept map.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Common Auxiliary Contractions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Auxiliary contractions are short words formed by the linking of the auxiliary verb and either a pronoun or the particle not. We use them in every day speech and informal writing. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>In the English language, there are certain auxiliaries that have contracted forms. In this occasion, we will focus on the contracted auxiliary forms of the simple present, present continuous, and simple past tenses.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>In the <strong>simple present </strong>and the<strong> present continuous</strong>, we use contractions with the verb to be in the following cases:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>When we use the affirmative form of the <strong>verb to be</strong>:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">am = <strong>'m</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">is =<strong> 's</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">are = <strong>'re</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>I&rsquo;<strong>m </strong>a software developer.</i></p> <p><i><strong>He's&nbsp;</strong>currently working on an open source project. </i></p> <p><i>They<strong>'re</strong> in charge of the project.&nbsp;</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>With the negative and interrogative form of the <strong>verb to be</strong>:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">is + not = <strong>isn&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">are + not = <strong>aren&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>He <strong>isn&rsquo;t </strong>currently working on an open source project.</i></p> <p><i>They <strong>aren&rsquo;t </strong>software developers. </i></p> <p><strong><i>Aren&rsquo;t</i></strong><i> you a software developer?</i></p> <p><strong><i>Isn&rsquo;t </i></strong><i>he studying for the programming test?</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>When we use other verbs different from the <strong>verb to be</strong> in the <strong>simple present</strong>, we use the auxiliary verbs <strong>do</strong> and <strong>does</strong> in contracted form with the negative and the interrogative forms:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">do + not = <strong>don&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">does + not =<strong>doesn&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>Open source Software <strong>doesn&rsquo;t</strong> have copyright restrictions.</i></p> <p><i>Copyright holders <strong>don&rsquo;t</strong> limit the purposes software can be used for.</i></p> <p><strong><i>Don&rsquo;t</i></strong><i> you know how open source software works?</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>For the <strong>simple past</strong>, we stick to the same rules as in the simple present. With the <strong>verb to be</strong> in past form, we use contractions in negative and interrogative sentences:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">was + not = <strong>wasn&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">were + not = <strong>weren&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>He <strong>wasn&rsquo;t</strong> aware of what an open source project was.</i></p> <p><i>They <strong>weren&rsquo;t sure</strong> about the concept of open source software. </i></p> <p><strong><i>Weren&rsquo;t</i></strong><i> they software developers?</i></p> <p><i>&nbsp;</i></p> <p>When we use other verbs different from the verb to be in the <strong>simple past</strong>, we use the auxiliary <strong>did</strong> in contracted form with the negative and the interrogative forms:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">did + not = <strong>didn&rsquo;t</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>He <strong>didn&rsquo;t </strong>know anything about open source software.</i></p> <p><i>They <strong>didn&rsquo;t </strong>use open source software at the time.</i></p> <p><strong><i>Didn&rsquo;t </i></strong><i>you know the open source movement?</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "No, I don't, this is the first time I hear about it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's even more than that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I didn't know a thing about them but now, I definitely want to get to know some of that kind of software.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Verb + infinitive: Questions with Would like to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>In English, there are some <strong>infinitive verbs</strong> that are always followed by other verbs such as the verb <strong>would like to. </strong></p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>These verbs are always followed by the preposition<strong> <i>to</i></strong> and they can express different meanings. <i><strong>Would like to</strong></i>&nbsp;refers to the desire or the intention of doing something:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>I <strong><i>would like to</i></strong> understand how a database software works.</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>You can use <i>verbs with infinitives </i>in affirmative or interrogative forms, for instance:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>I <strong><i>would like to</i></strong> see how to use free access software.</li> <li><strong><i>Would </i></strong>you <strong><i>like to</i></strong> know how to use free access software?</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Remember that you can use the contracted form of the verb too:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>I&rsquo;<strong><i>d like to </i></strong>see how to code using MySQL.</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>There are some other <i>infinitive verbs </i>with similar meaning as <i>would like to </i>such as <i>want to</i> or&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>The following is the structure to make questions using <strong>would like to</strong>:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Would</strong> + subject + <strong>like</strong> +<strong> to</strong> + &nbsp;<strong>verb in infinitive</strong> + complement?</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i><strong>Would</strong> you <strong>like to have</strong> free access to software without any restriction?</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Would you like to learn about it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Of course, in fact, would you like to go to the computer lab right now?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Open Source Software", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Open Source Software is a kind of computer software with a license in which the copyright holder provides permission to thirds to study, make changes and distribute the software to any person and for any purpose.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In the following chart, you have the top ten Open Source Software products.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Open Source Software</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Characteristics</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Apache Spark\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A tool that allows users to process big data sets across many nodes  while coordinating the processing, so. the users can concentrate on writing their queries in their language of choice.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Blender\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Blender Foundation aims to build a free and open source 3D creation pipeline for artists and small teams.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"D3\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It makes easier the visualization of big amounts of data.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Dolphin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A file manager with especial features to control quickly and easily your file system.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Git\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It allows tracking changes to files.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mattermost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A JavaScript based team chat system.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Piwik\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An open source alternative to google analytics.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"R\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A programming software aimed to statistical computing and graphics.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sugar CRM\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A tool that helps organizations to manage their contacts (customers).\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Vagrant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is a software to configure and command virtual machines.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can explain what the open source movement is.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify concepts and information related to the open source movement.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can obtain information about the open source movement.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you know about free license software?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What kind of open software projects do you know? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Getting to Know the Open Source Movement ", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "type": "WLC"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [5], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Two friends talk about Open Source Movement.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 1, "type": "STI"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "It doesn't promote the usage of free license software. ", "type": "text"}], "sel